1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:02,358
MACD looks complicated.

2
00:00:02,727 --> 00:00:05,768
It's really just two moving averages talking to each other.

3
00:00:06,268 --> 00:00:13,799
MACD is the gap between a fast and a slow moving average, usually the twelve and twenty six period EMA.

4
00:00:14,147 --> 00:00:16,562
When the fast one pulls away, the gap grows.

5
00:00:17,062 --> 00:00:20,324
The signal line is a smoothed version of MACD.

6
00:00:20,732 --> 00:00:27,660
When MACD crosses above it, momentum is turning up. When it crosses below, momentum is turning down.

7
00:00:28,160 --> 00:00:30,687
The histogram shows the distance between the two.

8
00:00:31,026 --> 00:00:33,555
Shrinking bars mean the momentum is fading.

9
00:00:34,055 --> 00:00:36,005
Like any moving average, it lags.

10
00:00:36,399 --> 00:00:40,204
And in choppy, sideways markets, it gives lots of false crosses.

11
00:00:40,704 --> 00:00:44,341
MACD is one of the Pro indicators on Meme Street.

12
00:00:44,715 --> 00:00:47,095
Practise reading it at memestreet.net.

